lesson: 203
title: Legs on birds, and animals with none
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: Every bird has 2 legs: chickens, ducks, penguins, owls and parrots stand on 2 legs.
explain: A snake has no legs at all, so snakes add nothing to a count of legs.
explain: 4 chickens and 3 snakes have 4 × 2 + 3 × 0 = 8 legs.
vars: a=name b=name n=2..15 s=2..9
answer: 2 * n
exercise: A farm has {n} chickens and {s} snakes in the long grass. How many legs do they have altogether?
exercise: At the zoo, {n} penguins live next to {s} snakes. How many legs are there in the two pens?
exercise: {a} counts {n} ducks and {s} snakes by the river. How many legs did {a.he} see?
exercise: In the bird house there are {n} parrots and the keeper brings in {s} snakes to show the class. How many legs are there?
exercise: How many legs do {n} owls and {s} snakes have together?
exercise: {a} and {b} see {s} snakes and {n} chickens on a farm visit. How many legs is that?
exercise: {n} chickens n {s} snakes in the reptile bit of the farm. legs?
exercise: zoo had {s} snakes, {n} penguins, the penguins were so cute omg. how many legs
exercise: {n+2} ducks, wait no {n} ducks on the pond and {s} snakes in the reeds?? how many legs
exercise: {a} says {s} snakes have heaps of legs. nah. {s} snakes and {n} parrots, legs?
exercise: my cousin's got {s} pet snakes and {n} chickens, nan hates it. how many legs all together
test: Find the number of legs on {s} snakes and {n} ducks.
test: There are {s} snakes in one tank and {n} chickens in the yard outside. Count the legs.
test: {b} draws {n} owls and {s} snakes, each with the right number of legs. How many legs does {b.he} draw?
test: What is the total number of legs, if a pet shop has {n} parrots and {s} snakes?
test: The reptile house has {s} snakes, and {n} penguins waddle past the window. How many legs is that in all?
test: legs on {s} snakes + {n} chickens?
test: {n} penguins and {s} snakes, oh and the snakes were asleep lol. legs total
exam: Determine the aggregate number of legs possessed by {n.words} chickens and {s.words} snakes.
exam: It is given that a zoological establishment houses {n} penguins and {s} snakes. Ascertain the total quantity of legs present among these animals.
exam: A riverside survey enumerates {s} snakes and {n} ducks. Compute the number of legs pertaining to all animals so enumerated.
exam: Whereas a collection consists of {n} owls and {s} snakes, state the cardinality of the set of their legs.
exercise: There were {n+1} chickens and {s} snakes on the farm, but the fox 'paid a visit' and one chicken didn't make it. How many legs are there now?
exercise: When Grandad passed away, {a} took in his {n} parrots and {s} snakes. How many legs do the pets have?
test: the bloody fox had one, {n} hens left n {s} grass snakes in the field. how many legs, don't be thick, snakes got none
